assistantcommentary to=functions.choose_action{\n\
  \"choice\": \"no\"\n\
}functions.choose_actioncommentary{\"success\":true,\"action_taken\":\"passed\",\"game_seq\":413,\"next_action_pending\":true,\"next_action_type\":\"GAME_COMBAT\",\"next_action_message\":\"Begin combat phase\",\"next_action_hint\":\"Call pass_priority\"}assistantanalysisCombat: attacks with all three again. Opponent has 2 life, no blockers (Warden is still there, can block one attacker). If they block Bolt Hound (2), we still deal 3 damage from Ardoz (1) + Irreverent (2) = 3, lethal. If they block another, still lethal. So we attack all.\n\
\n\
assistantcommentary to=functions.choose_action{\n\
  \"attackers\": \"all\"\n\
}functions.choose_actioncommentary{\"success\":true,\"action_taken\":\"declared_attackers\",\"game_seq\":414,\"next_action_pending\":true,\"next_action_type\":\"GAME_SELECT\",\"next_action_message\":\"Play instants and activated abilities\",\"next_action_hint\":\"Call get_action_choices or choose_action to see details, or pass_priority to continue.\"}assistantanalysisOpponent may respond with Spawning Pit ability. They have Spawning Pit with charge=1, can sacrifice a creature. They have Warden 2/2 still alive (if not sacrificed). They could sacrifice it to add second charge, then later create token. But they'd lose ability to block, but they already will take lethal damage anyway. So no point.\n\
\n\
Pass.\n\
\n\
assistantcommentary to=functions.choose_action{\n\
